		{
			dependencies: ["3660C09F3A4CA58C"]
			description: [
				"An Advanced Hive with an Expansion Box supports managed production and upgrades. A Simulator keeps bees inside, but the required flowering block must be presented correctly on a Feeding Slab."
				"Productivity, speed, breeding, filtering and gene-related upgrades do different jobs. Verify the installed upgrade tooltip and compare output before filling every hive with the same expensive set."
				"Use one labelled hive as the test case. When it works for a full cycle, copy the design; when it fails, diagnose flower, bee type, weather and output space in that order."
				"Advanced Hives accept upgrades and expansion boxes, but automation magnifies mistakes. Stabilise one occupied hive, verify output, and add upgrades gradually while watching space, flowers, weather exposure, and access."
			]
